WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.610
- [Announcer] Seeking secrets
is a social experiment

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.760
where strangers share
honest and complex truths.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.620
We ask that you treat the
participants with respect.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.670
Thank you for listening to their stories.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.910
- [1st Woman] My ex-boyfriend
said he would kill himself

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.450
if he wasn't with me.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.260
I call in my ex because he's gone.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.873
I've been feeling grief
for two months now.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.643
(gentle music)

00:00:35.699 --> 00:00:38.277
(telephone ringing)

00:00:38.277 --> 00:00:39.485
- [2nd Woman] You died.

00:00:39.485 --> 00:00:43.068
- [3rd Woman] A few
Months later, she died.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.280
- [4th Woman] I've lost loved ones

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.820
and I've also had friends who
have struggled significantly

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.630
with grief, but I can
never tell those friends

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:05.640
that I'm often very suicidal.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.790
I maintain this sunny disposition to hide

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.540
what I've been going through

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:14.560
but as they're coping
with loss, I'm coping

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.340
with the effects that losing my own life

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.693
might have on their life.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.783
- Oh no.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.840
I sit in the same position
as her, every single day.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.300
My mom who has done the most

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.410
for me I feel like I can't even tell her

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.880
how I feel sometimes because the times

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.320
where it's gotten really,
really bad seeing her feel

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.720
like she's going to lose
me has hurt me so bad.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.560
- Sometimes putting on a sunny disposition

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:57.090
is trying to protect other people

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.350
and sometimes it's also
trying not to address

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.510
maybe what's going on with me,

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.360
and so you use it as like a
hiding mechanism for yourself

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.560
as well as for other people.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.560
And it is a dangerous thing
to feel kind of that alone.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.713
I'd highly encourage this person

00:02:15.713 --> 00:02:18.300
that they might be surprised if they share

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.640
how they're feeling with their friends.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.100
- [5th Woman] When I
was like 12 years old me

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.730
and my two brothers were
told that my grandfather

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.380
had passed away of a heart attack.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:32.630
It was really sad, first like
death I had to go through

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.860
and then fast forward
like two years later,

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:38.600
maybe more than that I'm
snooping through my mom's phone

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.720
and I find her Reddit account

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.280
and on her Reddit account, she detailed

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:49.030
how my grandfather are
actually committed suicide.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.090
They just told me he had a heart attack

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.180
because they didn't wanna explain

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:54.280
the concept of suicide to me.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.540
He had died two years ago

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.830
but now I'm grieving all over again

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.950
and for something completely different.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.030
And I can't tell my family

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.140
- It must really hurt because they say

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.680
they can't tell other
people or tell their family.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.520
Like it hurts that they can't mourn

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:12.460
in the way they usually do.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.510
- I would understand why
she wouldn't wanna tell

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.240
her children how he actually did it

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:21.260
cause I know that suicide is
a very hard topic to discuss.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.010
- I can't imagine being
an adult trying to explain

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.750
really big topics to a kid because

00:03:29.619 --> 00:03:30.604
I don't know what I would do.

00:03:30.604 --> 00:03:33.620
The first death in my life

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:36.670
I wasn't told what actually happened.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.800
I actually was also told
it was a heart attack.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.180
It's almost like you
have to solve a puzzle

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.300
before you can grieve when it
comes to that kind of stuff.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.410
Especially when you're younger.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:48.060
For this specific person they didn't keep

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.120
that information from you to hurt you.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.833
It was to actually protect you.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:53.860
- [6th Woman] So I've grown up in

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.640
the Bible Belt my entire life

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.120
and earlier this year, my
cousin died by suicide.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.700
Previous to this, I removed myself

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.200
from religion it's probably
been about a year now

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.950
when the time came for
the funeral, all people

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.210
could keep saying and talking

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:13.760
about was thank goodness
he was saved two months

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.280
before he died.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.600
And they kept repeating it
over and over and over again.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.340
And in those moments I was so angry

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:24.560
because I know that
there were people there

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:27.603
at his funeral who thought
that he probably went to hell.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.040
- It's very unfortunate

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:40.277
at a time like a funeral
for people to discuss

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.400
things like that but that may
just be their way of coping.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.980
Suicide is a very hard thing
to conceptualize especially

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:52.080
when it's your loved ones.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.960
So relying on faith is
definitely something

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.980
that is an anchor for
a lot of people to get

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.280
through stuff like this.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.140
- After I lost my sister,
the judgment that I just saw

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.710
from the church when I
wasn't actively going back

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:10.483
after the loss, I just, oh
man, I relate to that so well.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:15.880
- [1st Man] My 15-year-old brother took

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.123
his own life three years ago.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:22.470
Everyday I struggled with forgiving him

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:26.413
because it seemed like a very
selfish and weak thing to do.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:33.790
- My dad took his own life two
days before my 10th birthday.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:35.963
And,

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.840
it ripped the family apart
pretty significantly.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:45.540
And I remember I had woken up
the night that he had passed

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:50.560
and I had dialed his number I was

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.246
like, "I just wanna talk to him so bad."

00:05:53.246 --> 00:05:54.773
And then I never did.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.070
And for the longest time I was

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:59.857
like, "that would've
made all the difference."

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:06.050
I find that I'm angriest
in moments of transition.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.940
So like graduating from high school or

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.070
getting a new job, moments where it's

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:16.910
like I wish he was here
to see what I'm doing.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.690
Maybe it's too easy to
say we all make mistakes

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.390
cause that's a pretty big mistake.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.020
- I hope he can forgive his brother

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:29.920
and more than forgive
is accept his suffering

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.210
and the choice he made

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:33.730
and life's different for everybody.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:38.543
And I think acceptance is like
the right path towards peace.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.870
- [1st Woman] My ex-boyfriend
said he would kill himself

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.470
if he wasn't with me.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:48.330
I call him my ex because he's gone.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.713
I've been feeling grief
for two months now.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:07.870
- Someone very close to me when
I was younger was suffering

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:10.300
with depression and was very suicidal

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:14.170
and I was really the only person that knew

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:15.960
what they were going through.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.420
I had went home and told my mom

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.330
because this time it was real.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.280
I never talked to her after that.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:27.440
I was receiving messages from my friend

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:30.591
about how much she hated
me for doing what I did.

00:07:30.591 --> 00:07:31.960
- [interviewer] If you could say something

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:35.223
to your 12-year-old self,
what would you tell her?

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:45.770
- I would say that I'm proud of her.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:51.450
- [7th Woman] I lost my
best friend from suicide

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:54.290
when I was 23.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:57.870
I used to do a of drugs
so I can see her again

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:02.413
and it was just crazy times
after I stopped doing drugs,

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.750
I kind of forgot about her

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.520
and then I think that's
better for me to forget

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.440
about her than actually think about her

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:14.863
because there's no point when
she's not even here anymore.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.503
- I feel sad for this person

00:08:17.503 --> 00:08:22.410
that they feel like they
should just forget about them.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.280
That that's gonna make it better.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.460
I can't imagine just forgetting
even the shirt I'm wearing

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:28.910
this is my husband's shirt.

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:30.620
I haven't gotten rid of anything

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:34.050
and I don't plan on
it, to forget anything.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:36.700
My husband hung himself

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.733
and to this day,

00:08:40.141 --> 00:08:42.370
it's almost like a video saved in my mind

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.830
of exactly walking in the house.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.000
I struggled a lot with
seeing him all the time

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.300
and that still happens at times.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:53.720
I'll be driving and I'll
look through my mirror

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.860
and look into my backseat

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:58.170
and I see him with a rope around his neck,

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.153
how I found him.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.170
I don't know, I wish
that I remembered more

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:06.483
of the happy stuff, but it's difficult.

00:09:08.178 --> 00:09:09.993
It's just like there.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:16.780
- [8th Woman] I had a
friend who passed away in

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:21.780
the winter of 2018 and on
the two-year anniversary

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:27.340
of his death, he came to me in a dream.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:31.400
And in this dream, he gave
me a really, really long hug

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:34.060
and then he told me, "I know that

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:36.340
this isn't okay to ask of you

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:41.120
but you could always join me
here, I'm always so lonely."

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.540
And I told him I can't because
there are too many things

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.600
that I have to look forward to.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.910
He told me, "that's okay,
just promise me we'll hang out

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:49.330
once you get here,"

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:52.293
and I think about that
dream at least once a week.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:57.820
- So I actually have so
many dreams about my friend.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.610
She comes to me at least like once a month

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:02.927
but it's the same dream every single time.

00:10:02.927 --> 00:10:05.320
And I see her and I'm
like, "oh my God, Maya,"

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:06.630
like, "where have you been?"

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.000
Like, "I miss you so much."

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.770
And she's like, "I've been in school,"

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.370
and she's always in school.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:14.190
I graduated college almost a year ago.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.620
She would've graduated at the same time.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.510
But she's still in college in my head

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.940
since she never really graduated, I guess.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:24.370
- I hope that dream fades for her, I guess

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:28.970
because I know my husband is happy

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:31.420
for me of how far I've come.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.820
It's not been an easy one since he passed,

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.710
but I know that he wouldn't
want me to join him just yet.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:39.630
I know my husband is somewhere

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:43.750
where his heart is at peace

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:47.810
and I know he's painting
somewhere, listening to music,

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:52.810
probably Mac Demarco or Kid
Cudi having probably a taco.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.930
- It's really easy to say it gets better.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:58.103
We need to say that to each other I think.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:01.430
But it's really hard to believe

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:04.880
or to understand that it does get better.

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:07.127
Cause people would say
that to me all the time

00:11:07.127 --> 00:11:09.010
and like you wanna slap them.

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:12.080
I once woke up in like
a pool of my own blood.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.430
I remember being a little
upset that I woke up.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.227
But I'm so glad I did.

